&lt;li&gt;Applied industry experience building forecasts in messy real world settings where details, confounds, and the validity of assumptions matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A graduate degree in Data Science, Statistics, Economics, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent demonstrated expertise in formal analytical techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to connect technical results to real-world recommendations, and to translate product and business changes into technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of SQL, Python, AI analysis tools, and data/analytics engineering ecosystems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to distill complex quantitative work into crisp, actionable insights for diverse audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
